<<~ ahu slot=`#/checklist`>>

!! DAM checklist

The split moved `LarDiskProjector` (2,536 lines) into modules under `packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector/`, each wrapped by a heleuma code-meme; the class stays as the composer and its public surface carries every caller unchanged. Line counts name the files as the shore cut left them. The "pono?" column records what the split SAW; it prescribes no change.

|!module (code-meme) |!lines |!does, holds, carries |!callers |!pono? (seen) |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-composer`>> `disk-projector.ts` | 369 | composes the modules; holds the shared state; carries every public method as a one-line hand-off | island-behaviors, shore-verb, index barrel, node tests | Held state: the projector's memory of a file rests in the base alone; no per-file lifecycle map or reading counter stands in the composer. Internal fields moved from `private` to `protected` so the modules reach them through one cast (`core()`, `as unknown as ProjectorCore`); tests reach internals by cast (`flush`, `reconcile`, `atomicWrite`, `gate`, `_tw5`, `reconcileWatches`, `settleWakes`, `settleInboxes`), so those stay instance members, and `_scheduleUnlinkByTitle` keeps an instance hand-off because tests call it on the instance. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-options`>> `disk-projector/options.ts` | 206 | names every construction port | composer, core | Exception list: optional ports, each with its own "Absent →" fallback sentence. The alert rail splits by kind: `onRefusal` (a disk-ward refusal, a refused capture riding it) and `onPendingRemoval` / `onPendingRemovalResolved`; `capture` names the island's capture door. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-core`>> `disk-projector/core.ts` | 86 | names the shared state and the instance methods modules call back through | every module | Patch seam: the interface restates each field type by hand; the composer types most fields as `ProjectorCore[...]` to close the drift, and the cast through `unknown` would hide any mismatch that remains. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-entries`>> `disk-projector/entries.ts` | 85 | holds shared shapes (the moved file, the capture outcome), keys, alert title, file mode, path readers | every module, composer re-exports | `keepSpares` (the static `kept` renamed, since a local `let kept` shadowed it) takes `string or set`: two call shapes for one question. `rootOf` wraps `rootAddressOf` and adds nothing. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-start`>> `disk-projector/start.ts` | 129 | subscribes, opens the queue, marks mount-scan roots; stops | composer | Clock: the change handler stamps `performance.now()` into the measure; it annotates and never decides. Five mount-scan sources mark roots (own-record stores, tombstones, every wiki title, orphan flags, orphan folders). Duck-typed `listTombstoned` and `as never` casts reach past the store and wiki types. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-reconcile`>> `disk-projector/reconcile.ts` | 137 | reconciles one root; holds the residency bar and pack suppress | composer, agreement, dropped, orphans, flush, start | Exception list: `neverOnDisk` bars effect records and the temp layer's internal titles; the pack-member suppress rides first as a loop-stopper. One view pass serves every mirror: the draft and temp layers reconcile as ordinary mirrors. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-flush`>> `disk-projector/flush.ts` | 199 | renders, sites, settles left homes, skips identical bytes, writes, sweeps | composer, capture | A ladder of early returns. `debugJson` writes a peek beside the carrier outside every gate (stated as the projector's own artifact). `_firstFlushDone` latches once. `metaBody!` asserts what `metaPath !== null` implies. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-capture`>> `disk-projector/capture.ts` | 163 | hashes before the write and acts on the gate's answer; hands a moved file to the capture door | flush, homes | Patch-on-patch: the gate weighs twice, with a tree reread between, because a sibling may have moved the base. `headed` mutates inside the `baseOf` closure (held state in a closure). A refused capture writes nothing and rides `onRefusal`; the next reading weighs the file afresh. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-siting`>> `disk-projector/siting.ts` | 109 | sites a carrier; lists the files a siting holds | flush, dropped | The uniquifier caps its walk at 1000 tries. `sited` (in the composer) holds the last siting per mirror for the session alone; the base answers across a restart. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-write`>> `disk-projector/write.ts` | 77 | writes atomically; reads disk text; resolves pointer bytes | flush, capture, agreement, settle-word, composer | Clock: `noteFirstWrite` reads `performance.now()` to print one diagnostic line past a second; nothing paces on it. Read errors collapse to null (absent). |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-bases`>> `disk-projector/bases.ts` | 91 | answers document, lineage and base questions; pins and forgets | flush, capture, homes, pending, dropped, orphans, agreement | `docOf` coerces an empty document id to undefined with `||`. HEAD stands in for a base the re-found cleared, and pins nothing itself. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-homes`>> `disk-projector/homes.ts` | 111 | judges each unlink; unlinks agreed homes; hands a held home to capture | flush, dropped | `judgeHome` answers four verdicts plus a `behind` flag. Binary detection reads a utf8 round trip. An unreadable file reads `held: unreadable`, so it stays. A lone sidecar proves nothing and stays. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-pending`>> `disk-projector/pending.ts` | 113 | holds pending removals; surfaces each set at drain; senses the disk | composer, removals, capture, flush, reconcile | No clock: surfacing waits on the queue's idle handshake behind a `pendingMoved` latch. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-removals`>> `disk-projector/removals.ts` | 110 | answers remove or restore for pending carriers | composer | A seven-member refusal union. The count check refuses an answer over carriers its giver never read; the removal reads back from the view rather than trusting the door. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-dropped`>> `disk-projector/dropped.ts` | 108 | unlinks a dropped carrier per mirror; follows the kāpae shadow | reconcile, flush | Name drift: `_scheduleUnlinkByTitle` schedules nothing; it runs awaited in line. Tests call it on the instance, so the composer keeps a hand-off by that name. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-orphans`>> `disk-projector/orphans.ts` | 151 | writes orphan slot files, raises the flag, gives the folder back | start, reconcile | Swallowed errors: `unlinkSync` and `rmdirSync` failures pass silent (best-effort, a hand cleans up). |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-untracked`>> `disk-projector/untracked.ts` | 67 | keeps untracked files with one alert each; lists them for the census | dropped, composer | CRUD on `$:/temp` alert tiddlers straight through `addTiddler` and `deleteTiddler` on the wiki. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-agreement`>> `disk-projector/agreement.ts` | 106 | pins agreements it reads itself; folds the records' render | composer | `recordsRenderOf` chooses the render as reconcile chooses (the view's winner, else a shadowed own record that still projects). |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-settle-word`>> `disk-projector/settle-word.ts` | 188 | waits until a gesture's projection ran | composer | No clock: a handshake with change events and the drain. One look loop of ~64 lines ends on two breaks (every carrier answered or the projector stopping; a look after the far side closed); `closed = false as boolean` defeats narrowing on purpose. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-watches`>> `disk-projector/watches.ts` | 72 | arms wakes; watches the next reconcile; lists what the queue owes | start, settle-word, composer | `failedRoots` holds every root whose last reconcile threw until one lands; `reconcileWatched` rethrows after marking. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-disk-files`>> `disk-projector/disk-files.ts` | 85 | lists a carrier's files; reads which title owns a path | flush, siting, composer re-exports | Directory and parse errors collapse to empty or unknown; `.kapae` and `.orphans` take explicit exclusions. |
| <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-orphan-files`>> `disk-projector/orphan-files.ts` | 30 | serializes an orphan record; maps its slot path | orphans, composer re-exports | A deny set strips host and draft fields; a newline in a value or a colon in a name routes the record to JSON. |

!!! The shore cut ~ what it closes, what stays open

The operator's ruling (2026-11-28) holds the projector to rendering: siting, render, byte-identity skip, atomic write, unlink, and the hash before each write (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law`>>). A file a hand moved goes to the island's capture door (`packages/lararium-node/src/disk-capture.ts`), and the CRDT merges from there.

''Closes.''
* The composer holds no per-file lifecycle maps and no reading counter; the base alone carries what the projector knows of a file.
* Each module carries its work's name: `capture.ts` weighs a moved file (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-capture`>>), and `agreement.ts` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-agreement`>>) holds `pinAgreement` and `recordsRenderOf` alone.
* The recovery pass ahead of the view pass, and the loop fix it carried, left reconcile: the draft and temp layers project as ordinary mirrors, and no `mirrorClass` stands.
* The three-port alert split (`onRefusal`, `onConflict`, `onConflictResolved`) narrowed to `onRefusal` and the pending-removal pair; a refused capture rides `onRefusal`.

''Stays open.''
* The weigh-twice patch in `capture.ts` (a tree reread between two weighings) and the `headed` closure state.
* `_scheduleUnlinkByTitle` still schedules nothing; the instance hand-off stands for the tests that call it.
* The windows' source tiddlers (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/source/disk-projector-…`) still ship in no carrier (see #/registration).
* `disk-capture.ts` rests beside the projector, outside `disk-projector/`, as island wiring; it carries no code-meme of its own, and its header points at the disk-projection law.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/registration`>>

!! Heleuma registration

`packages/lararium-tw5/scripts/sync-heleuma.ts` reads every mesh anchor whose `source-file` names a node-package module: the window check (module-ref declared, window standing, window facing the ref) and a `source-sha256` check against the file's bytes. Drift warns and never blocks; `build:heleuma:commit` restamps. Each window faces `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/source/disk-projector-…`, a source tiddler no carrier ships yet: the wave crest ships its source as a `.tid` in the TW5 plugin, and packing the projector's node-only source into the browser plugin waits on its own decision.

<<~/ahu>>

